{
  "_comment": [
    "The rollback wire format, frozen. Two keys, one invariant each way: a type",
    "may not join it unseen, and a type that leaves must be PRUNED here in the",
    "same commit. That second half is what makes this a ratchet and not a budget.",
    "",
    "\u26a0 RENAMED `central_codecs` -> `encoded_types` on 2026-07-30 (slice F). The",
    "old key named a FILE \u2014 `ambition_platformer2d_runtime/src/rollback/codecs.rs` \u2014 because",
    "the orphan rule forced ~100 foreign impls into it: the trait sat above every",
    "crate whose types it encoded. Slice F moved the trait to the floor",
    "(`ambition_platformer2d_core::snapshot`) and the impls home to their own crates.",
    "",
    "\u26a0 The rename found a blind spot rather than causing one. All 62 previously",
    "frozen types are still present; the count went to 63 because `MotionModel`",
    "was encoded in `motion_codec.rs`, a SECOND file the single-file collector",
    "never read. A guard that says 'the wire format' while reading one of two",
    "files is the failure this repo keeps rediscovering \u2014 it was green, and it",
    "was green about less than it claimed.",
    "\u26a0 S4 (2026-07-30) added five entries, and they are a JOIN rather than a drift: FighterStocks and FighterEliminated are the stocks loop's own state \u2014 a stock count that is not rollback state UN-SPENDS itself on a rewind, so a fighter loses the same stock twice or never loses it at all \u2014 plus message.body_knocked_out and message.fighter_stock_spent, which must be CLEARED on load or a rewound KO is re-read and spends a second stock. derived.resolved_combat_tuning is AE6's projection, declared derived rather than registered as state on purpose: restoring it independently of the declaration that produced it is the borrow the seam removed.",
    "\u26a0 S4's match-end half (2026-07-31) joins two more: StocksMatchSettled is the 'already announced' latch, registered as STATE rather than left a Local because a rewind across the deciding frame must be able to UN-decide the match \u2014 a latch that survived it would swallow the re-announcement on the replay and the ruleset would never hear the match end. message.stocks_match_decided is cleared on load for the same reason.",
    "\u26a0 SR-0 (2026-08-04) adds rollback encodings for accumulated proper time and the derived 2D relativity sample; TwinTrack is the concrete acceptance game.",
    "\u26a0 SR-1 (2026-08-05) adds canonical coordinate time, proper-time cooldown, emitter, receiver/pool configuration, analytic light-signal, and bounded arrival-history encodings. The joins are deliberate: course rules depend on emission identity, passbands, deterministic slot allocation, cooldown state, and event history surviving rewind.",
    "\u26a0 SR-2 (2026-08-05) adds canonical optical-source and observer declarations while keeping the optical view and worldline reconstruction derived.",
    "\u26a0 SR-3 (2026-08-05) adds the canonical RelativisticTarget2d declaration used by exact constant-velocity null-intercept targeting. TwinTrack aim, view mode, pursuit timing, and hit results are carried inside its existing canonical experiment component and require rollback schema v10.",
    "\u26a0 Cutscene playback joins the wire format (2026-08-06). ActiveCutscene::is_playing() drives a CAPTURING input-context claim, so whether the participant can act is gameplay truth rather than the \"scripted presentation sequence state\" the rollback_coverage waiver calls it \u2014 a rewind into a playing frame that did not restore it would let the resimulation act through beats the original could not. The codec encodes the SEMANTIC half only (script, beat index, elapsed, finished); dialogue line, banner, camera target and fade alpha are derived and re-published by the tick. \u2714 REGISTERED 2026-08-06 as `cutscene.playback`, OPTIONAL-canonical because a composition without cutscenes carries no ActiveCutscene and the plain form's checksum system panics on a missing resource. Schema v10 -> v11: a v10 peer cannot reconstruct whether the participant was allowed to act.",
    "\u26a0 SCHEMA v16 (2026-08-08) added six entries, and every one of them is a JOIN: the narrative boundary. actor.pending_challenge + map.pending_challenge are an ARMED challenge counting down to a fight \u2014 a sim system removes it, so a rewind past that removal kept the removal and disarmed the fight. message.conversation_ended, message.challenge_requested, message.item_grant_requested and message.shop_transaction_requested are what the non-rewound Yarn runner tells the simulation, released from the conversation ledger on the tick they were stamped for and cleared on load so a resimulated tick is HANDED them rather than remembering them. Three of the four had no message at all before: <<give_item>>, <<buy_item>> and <<challenge>> reached into rollback state from Update.",
    "\u26a0 SCHEMA v17 (2026-08-08) adds actor.active_combatant, and it is a JOIN with a lifecycle the markers beside it do not have: RulesetOwnsDeath is attached at seating and never removed, while this one is REMOVED on elimination. A rewind past an elimination has to put it back, or the replayed branch runs with a fighter that is out of a match it has not lost yet. It replaces TWO proxies \u2014 RulesetOwnsDeath in CombatStanding::of and Has<MatchSeat> in the stand-down guard \u2014 neither of which meant 'is this body in a fight'.",
    "\u26a0 v18 (2026-08-08) is the TwinTrack Relativity Plaza/Festival overlay, merged rather than unpacked: it was cut 2026-08-06 from a branch predating a301a79a0, so main's newer relativity API won where the two disagreed. \u26a0 NOTHING CHANGES IN THIS FILE FOR IT, and that is the point worth writing down: this ratchet reads the RUNTIME's registrations (rollback/registry.rs + rollback/domains/**), and every `twintrack.*` name is registered by the demo crate, which the scanner never reads. The live dump in game/ambition_app/tests/rollback_schema_baseline.txt is the one that moves \u2014 it recorded twintrack.chase_beacon leaving and twintrack.character joining. Adding a demo-side name here reports STALE immediately, because the scanner cannot see it."
  ],
